# ~/.skhdrc snippet for same-window-switcher (ANSI US)
#
# One-shot CLI: the binary has no hotkeys. skhd launches next/prev.
#
# Use keycodes, not a literal grave/backtick — skhd's parser breaks on it.
# ANSI US physical grave is 0x32. Confirm with: skhd --observe
#
# JIS and other layouts: run `skhd --observe` and bind the keycode you see.
# Do not guess. This file does not publish a JIS keycode.
#
# Disable System Settings → Keyboard → Keyboard Shortcuts → Keyboard →
# "Move focus to next window" first, or the OS will steal the chord.
#
# Absolute path required. skhd's PATH is not your login shell.
# Primary install:  make install      → $HOME/.local/bin/same-window-switcher
# Fallback (Tahoe): make install-app  → $HOME/Applications/SameWindowSwitcher.app
#   then point at Contents/MacOS/same-window-switcher
#
# AeroSpace cmd-grave may not be the same physical key as skhd 0x32.
# Grant Accessibility to THIS binary (or the .app), not skhd.
# Key-repeat is serialized by flock; wait is OK.

cmd - 0x32 : $HOME/.local/bin/same-window-switcher next
cmd + shift - 0x32 : $HOME/.local/bin/same-window-switcher prev

# After make install-app, use the bundle binary instead:
# cmd - 0x32 : $HOME/Applications/SameWindowSwitcher.app/Contents/MacOS/same-window-switcher next
# cmd + shift - 0x32 : $HOME/Applications/SameWindowSwitcher.app/Contents/MacOS/same-window-switcher prev
